    <h2 style="font-size:1.6rem;font-weight:300;color:#fff;margin-bottom:1.5rem;">How to Verify Any Manufacturer Before You Commit</h2>
    <p style="color:#ddd;line-height:1.8;font-size:0.92rem;margin-bottom:1rem;">Whatever you go with, check it before you commit. Ask for a business registration number and look it up (RJSC and BGMEA, for a Bangladesh factory). Ask if you can visit or audit in person. And get it in writing whether the factory making your sample is the same one that will make your bulk order — that one question alone rules out a lot of bad options. For a longer list of warning signs, see our guide on <a href="/insights/avoiding-clothing-manufacturer-scams" style="color:#e00;text-decoration:none;">spotting a fake clothing manufacturer</a>.</p>
